// MCLA GPU renderer -- the blue noise tile the screen-space effects sample with (blue_noise.h): a void-and-cluster tile of 32 x 32 pixels, one byte a pixel
// (the top 8 bits of its rank: each of the 256 levels in four pixels, so the noise (level + 0.5) / 256 is uniform), four to a word, pixel 4 w in the low byte.
// The second channel is the same tile read 13 pixels right and 8 down.
//
// WRITTEN by `larecomp_blue_noise_test --emit` from blue_noise.h and checked against it by the same test (src/gpu/blue_noise_test.cpp): do not edit by hand.
// The lookup is plain enough to compile as C++ (the test does, and so does ssr_test.cpp).

